1. Qt 6.11.1 (Community Edition)
   Upstream:  https://www.qt.io/qt-technologies
              https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/6.11/6.11.1/submodules/
   License:   LGPL-3.0-only (used via dynamic linking; Qt also offers
              GPL/commercial alternatives, and this project uses the LGPL
              route).
   Usage:     Dynamically linked Qt modules Core, Gui, Widgets, Concurrent,
              Svg, Multimedia and MultimediaWidgets; LinguistTools is used
              at build time only. Qt Network is pulled in transitively by
              Qt Multimedia at runtime. Qt is dynamically linked and its
              DLLs are replaceable by the user; no end-user license term
              restricts reverse engineering needed to debug modifications to
              LGPL-licensed Qt. QtSvg 6.11.1 is rebuilt with the five official
              CVE-2026-8168 patches. The provenance record shipped with the
              binary (QtSvg-security-provenance.txt) lists the patch names and
              SHA-256 hashes, while the patch URLs, the source-archive URL and
              hash, the verification steps and the complete build recipe live
              in this repository: tools/build_patched_qtsvg.ps1 pins the
              official QtSvg 6.11.1 source archive and the five official patch
              files by URL and SHA-256, verifies each with git apply --check
              before applying, and builds with CMake and Ninja, so the exact
              patched QtSvg can be rebuilt from this repository. See also
              legal/QT_LGPL_RELINKING.md.

